    // A parameter separator is any character that cannot be part of a
    // parameter name.  Valid characters for a name are alphanumerics,
    // underscore, hyphen and dot.  Whitespace and common punctuation are
    // treated as separators.  Any other non‑ASCII character is also
    // considered a separator.
    if (c == '\0') {
